/T (A trained Naive Bayes classifier learns word patterns from labelled complaints and estimates the likely sentiment class. A pre-trained language model can understand richer context but usually needs more memory and processing time. A lexicon scorer is lightweight and takes approximately O\(w\) time for w words. A trained model's inference cost depends on its vocabulary/features or model size. Accuracy must be compared using labelled test complaints; a more complex model is not automatically better. )
