/P 178 0 R
/T (An unsafe query is created by joining a user-provided station name directly into the SQL text. An input such as Adyar' OR '1'='1 can change the meaning of the WHERE condition and may cause the query to return records that were not requested. A safe query uses a ? placeholder and passes the station name separately as a parameter. SQLite then treats the entire string as a literal station name, not as executable SQL. Since no station has that exact name, the expected result is None. )
/E (An unsafe query is created by joining a user-provided station name directly into the SQL text. An input such as Adyar' OR '1'='1 can change the meaning of the WHERE condition and may cause the query to return records that were not requested. A safe query uses a ? placeholder and passes the station name separately as a parameter. SQLite then treats the entire string as a literal station name, not as executable SQL. Since no station has that exact name, the expected result is None. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [11]
