/E (Keep the lexicon scorer as a transparent baseline; test a trained classifier if measured accuracy is insufficient. Measure accuracy on labelled complaints; use human review for ambiguous or high-impact cases. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
741 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (The simple lexicon method is fast and easy to explain but does not reliably understand sarcasm, complex negation, mixed sentiment or Tamil-English language. A trained model may improve context handling, but it requires labelled examples, testing, monitoring and more memory/processing. Choose the model based on measured agreement and error analysis rather than assuming that a complex model is automatically better. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
