743 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (The assignment also asks what happens if a summariser selects the first k sentences rather than choosing sentences with the most frequent important words. Selecting the first k can be quick, but it may omit the central complaint if the important issue appears later. Frequency-based selection requires scanning the words, counting them and scoring sentences, so it takes work proportional to the number of words \(plus ranking the sentences\). The first-k method may use less computation, but it generally gives less relevant summaries. Compare both methods on the same 50 complaints and judge whether the key issue, location and requested action are retained. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
