/Title (Using print statements for every row can create thousands of console writes. Console output is relatively slow and can increase total runtime. Logging is more flexible because levels such as DEBUG, INFO, WARNING and ERROR can be configured. A production run can suppress DEBUG and INFO messages while retaining warnings and errors. Breakpoints and interactive debugging are disabled simply by running the normal program without the debugger. Temporary prints should be removed or guarded by a debug setting. The real overhead depends on machine and terminal, so compare timings rather than assuming a fixed cost.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1482 0 R
/Next 1493 0 R
>>
endobj
